{'symbol': 'MRK', 'date': '2022-09-09 08:00:00', 'title': 'LYNPARZA® (OLAPARIB) IN COMBINATION WITH BEVACIZUMAB, AND AS MONOTHERAPY, DEMONSTRATES CLINICALLY MEANINGFUL LONG-TERM SURVIVAL IN CERTAIN PATIENTS WITH FIRST-LINE ADVANCED OVARIAN CANCER IN EXPLORATORY ANALYSES OF TWO PHASE 3 TRIALS', 'text': 'RAHWAY, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)---- $MRK #MRK--ASTRAZENECA AND MERCK, KNOWN AS MSD OUTSIDE OF THE UNITED STATES AND CANADA, TODAY ANNOUNCED LONG-TERM FOLLOW-UP RESULTS FROM THE PHASE 3 PAOLA-1 AND SOLO-1 TRIALS IN FIRST-LINE ADVANCED OVARIAN CANCER, WHICH REPRESENT THE LONGEST-TERM DATA FOR ANY PARP INHIBITOR IN THIS SETTING. THESE RESULTS WERE PRESENTED ON SEPT. 9 AT THE EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR MEDICAL ONCOLOGY (ESMO) 2022 CONGRESS, AND THE SOLO-1 RESULTS WERE PUBLISHED IN THE JOURNAL OF CLINICAL ONCOLOGY. OVARI'}